  en:{name:"English",nav:["Home","Categories","Product details","SEO articles","FAQ","Guides"],eyebrow:"Independent research preview",hero:"Research PikoBuy finds before you open a product link.",intro:"A category-led research desk for comparing product context, QC needs, sizing and parcel weight — then continuing to the live FindSpreadsheet record.",search:"Search products or paste a product name",searchBtn:"Search FindSpreadsheet",note:"This is an independent research guide. It does not sell products, take payments or manage orders.",method:"A calmer buying workflow",steps:["Choose one product category.","Compare photos, size context and item details.","Think about package weight before value.","Open the matching FindSpreadsheet result."],browse:"Browse the 10 research categories",browseText:"Each category leads to a focused FindSpreadsheet route, not a dead-end card.",check:"What this site checks first",checkIntro:"The useful difference is not a longer list — it is a better question before each click.",checks:["QC photo coverage for the category","Size chart or measurement context","Source and product-detail match","Weight and parcel-planning context"],facts:"What the PikoBuy workflow means",factsIntro:"PikoBuy describes a workflow of selecting a source item or link, warehouse inspection, then choosing and paying for international shipping. This guide turns those steps into research checks, without making service promises.",fact:["Source-first","Start with the item name or original listing, not a slogan." ,"Warehouse-aware","Plan to check photos and details before parcel submission.","Shipping-aware","Treat route, dimensions and weight as decision inputs."],go:"Open FindSpreadsheet",page:{categories:["Category research", "Choose the item type first. Each page tells you what evidence matters, then sends you to the matching FindSpreadsheet category."],products:["Product details before product links","Use this page to decide which details deserve attention before opening a product record."],articles:["Evidence-led PikoBuy guides","These are the SEO clusters that can outperform generic spreadsheet copy: each answers one buyer question with a clear next step."],faq:["PikoBuy research FAQ","Clear boundaries make a useful research site more trustworthy than a page full of uncheckable promises."],guides:["The PikoBuy research method","Use the official platform flow as a checklist: select an item, confirm details, review warehouse information, then choose a shipping route."]},qa:[["What should I check before opening a find?","Start with category fit, useful photos, visible sizing information, product-detail match and expected parcel weight."],["Is this an official PikoBuy website?","No. This is an independent research preview that helps users find records on FindSpreadsheet. It does not represent PikoBuy."],["Can this site quote final shipping or guarantee delivery?","No. Final shipping, customs, carrier and order questions depend on the account and route involved."],["Why do product details matter?","A list title alone cannot confirm measurements, options, photo coverage or shipping impact."]],cards:["QC photo checklist","How to inspect photos by product type before a record moves to your shortlist.","Sizing and measurement guide","A category-based way to compare fit notes before choosing a size.","Shipping weight planning","How item weight, packaging and dimensions can change the final decision."],labels:{research:"Research",details:"Details to review",open:"Open category",back:"Back to research",summary:"Buyer checklist"}},
